 "text": "Home - Howard County Business & Tourism -->\nHome - Howard County Business & Tourism\nYou are using an outdated browser. Please upgrade your browser .\nMENU MENU\nCommunities\nCity of Chester\nCity of Cresco\nCity of Elma\nCity of Lime Springs\nCity of Protivin\nCity of Riceville\nBusinesses\nWhy Howard County?\nBusiness Directory\nEconomic Development\nStarting A Business\nBusiness Resources\nTourism\nUpcoming Events\nThings to Do\nPlaces to Stay\nCommunity Festivals\nTourism Resources\nAbout Howard County\nDepartments\nMoving Here\nInteresting People & Places\nResidents\nEmployment\nRental Properties & More\nVeterans\nCOVID-19 Info\nFarmers Markets\nResident Resources\nContact Us\nCourtney 2400cook DixBunyDi1k Unsplash\nCattle 4103391\nDave Hoefler H8bnRXmN33I Unsplash\nDave Hoefler YWcy3iq1HqQ Unsplash\nMove Here\nVisit Us\nStart A Business\nEmployment\nLocal\nHoward County Businesses\nHoward County is home to many innovative and unique businesses like Featherlite, Inc. Visitor can enjoy the largest flower and produce market in the region (Cedar Valley), Amish and Mennonite greenhouses and shops, the first county-wide Farmers Market in the state of Iowa.\nBusiness Directory\nTlusty Detailing\nRiceville Community Center\n10th Hole Inn & Suites\n1\n2\nLodging\nAttractions\nRestaurants\nFestivals\nRetail\nInfluencers\nTourism\nExperience Howard County\nHistory buffs can visit the boyhood home and farm of Dr. Norman Borlaug, learn why we are so proud of Ellen Church , and stop in at the Iowa Wrestling Hall of Fame .\nOutdoor enthusiasts can enjoy canoeing, snowmobiling, cross country skiing, hiking, off-road trails, and miles of bike trails. Take some time to explore Lake Hendricks in Riceville and the Nature Center at Vernon Springs. We have dirt track racing, three golf courses, and excellent hunting & fishing opportunities.\nEnjoy a run or walk on one of our many bike trails. Work-out along the trail with by using our strategically placed outdoor equipment along the Prairie Springs Recreation Trail . This scenic experience adds a challenge to all fitness levels.\nDon’t miss a stop at the largest fitness center in the region featuring an indoor pool, hot tub, track, basketball court, weights, and virtual golf.\nGather with us at one (or all) of our city summer festivals or experience an Iowa winter trip to celebrate Snowfest in January.\nResidents\nChamber & Courthouse\nThe Cresco Chamber of Commerce is a community within itself. It brings its members together to not only benefit the community but also to benefit each other. Through various events, you will meet, network, and connect with a wide array of influential professionals.\nThe Howard County Courthouse in Cresco, Iowa, United States was built in 1880. It was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1981 as a part of the County Courthouses in Iowa Thematic Resource. The courthouse is the third building the county has used for court functions and county administration.\nMore Info\nMore Info\nStay Informed\nNews & Events\n18\nOct\nSunday Movies at Cresco Theatre\nSunday , Cresco Theatre & Opera House\nEVENT DETAIL\n19\nOct\nNo School – Professional Development Day at Howard-Winn\nMonday , Howard-Winn School District\nEVENT DETAIL\n19\nOct\nWellbeing & Community Health Clinic\nMonday , Cresco Fitness Center\nEVENT DETAIL\n19\nOct\nAA Meeting\nMonday , VFW Hall\nEVENT DETAIL\nNo event found!\nAll Events\nIowa Travel Industry Partners / iTIP\nFebruary 3, 2023\n2021 Laborshed Area Analysis\nFebruary 2, 2023\nAll News & Resources\nHoward County Business & Tourism\n101 2nd Ave SW\nCresco, Iowa 52136\n(563) 547 - 3434\nContact Us\nCopyright © 2026 - Howard County Business & Tourism. | All Rights Reserved.\nPowered by Iroc Web Design Services .\nTop",
